  "raw": {
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Postdoctoral-Fellow_R000024286": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n- Salary package:  $112,550 - $120,621 (A.6-A.8) per annum plus 17% employer's superannuation and annual leave loading  - Appointment Type: Full-time, fixed term appointment for 2 years  - Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde  The role    We are seeking a Postdoc toral Fellow, to join our category theory group. This position is associated with Dr. Jean-Simon Pacaud Lemay's AFOSR grant FA9550-24-1-0008. As such, the successful applicant will work in the area of differential categories, tangent categories, and other category theory related topics, whether th is be for mathematics (such as for differential geometry, algebraic geometry, etc.) or for computer science (such as machine learning, linear logic, etc.).    While the position start date is flexible, the successful applicant must have completed their PhD prior to commencing the role. The position can commence at any time during 2027, with the appointment being for a period of two years from the successful applicant’s commencement date.   About you (Selection Criteria)   PhD (or soon completed a PhD) in mathematics, computer science, or related areas.    Research experience in, related to, or applications of category theory.    Why Join Us?   Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today .   We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Take a look at the fabulous staff benefits on offer when you work at Macquarie University.   How to Apply To be considered, please apply online and submit :    A Cover Letter, which includes the name of two references and, if applicable, the expected end date of your PhD.   Your Resume   A r esearch proposal, 3-page max (excluding references).   *This position requires a criminal history and qualifications check.   Applications Close: Friday 16 th of October at 11:59pm (AEST) 2026.  We welcome applications from international candidates.  For enquiries or a confidential conversation:   P lease contact JS Lemay – Senior Lecturer at js.lemay@mq.edu.au .     The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion.   Pre-Employment Checks    Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will  be required  to  participate  in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.    Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 16/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Research-Fellow_R000024316": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - China Studies",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-29\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nShape Australia's understanding of contemporary China and pursue impactful research and inform national policy conversations. · Salary Package: From Level A.1 ($89,579) to A.6 ($112,550) per annum, plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading. · Full-time, fixed-term (12-month residential position) · Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde About the Fellowship The China Strategic Knowledge Initiative at Macquarie University invites applications for a full-time Postdoctoral Research Fellowship commencing in 2027. This is a12-month, residential position based at Macquarie University in Sydney designed to support emerging scholars whose research informs Australia’s understanding of contemporary China. There will be two additional 12-month fellowships available in the future, one in 2028 and one in 2029. This fellowship is intended to strengthen policy-relevant scholarship and public engagement on China’s foreign policy, security, defence, and domestic politics. The successful candidate will contribute to research excellence while actively engaging and informing government, media, and the broader policy community. This fellowship offers a unique opportunity for an early-career scholar to develop a strong research profile while contributing to Australia’s public and policy conversations on China. Eligible applicants with a demonstrated commitment to scholarly excellence and public engagement are strongly encouraged to apply. About the Role Based in the Faculty of Arts at Macquarie University in Sydney, you will join a vibrant intellectual community with access to the University's research resources, working under the mentorship and guidance of Associate Professor Courtney Fung, PhD, and Honorary Professor Bates Gill, PhD. The fellowship is structured across two areas: - 80% Research (approximately four days per week): Independent and joint research aligned with the Initiative's mission. You will be expected to make significant progress in refining and publishing the results of your PhD thesis research. - 20% Engagement (approximately one day per week): Public and policy engagement activities, planned in consultation with your fellowship advisors. These may include: Policy briefings and consultations Policy papers and opinion pieces Media commentary and public outreach Participation in workshops, seminars, and public events Contributions to Australian policy discussions regarding China Eligibility: Applications are open to Australian citizens and permanent residents. You must be able to live and work in Australia for the duration of the fellowship. About Us Established in 2026, the China Strategic Knowledge Initiative is supported by the National Foundation for Australia-China Relations and Macquarie University. It aims to build Australia's knowledge base and policy engagement on China through rigorous scholarship and meaningful public outreach. More information about CSKI and the fellowship program is available at https://www.mq.edu.au/faculty-of-arts/schools/school-of-international-<br>studies/our-research/china-strategic-knowledge-initiative. About You (Selection Criteria) You are an early-career scholar with a demonstrated commitment to scholarly excellence and public engagement, ready to develop a strong research profile and help shape Australia's understanding of contemporary China. You bring rigour to your research and enthusiasm for sharing your expertise with government, media, and the wider policy community. A completed PhD (or thesis submitted) relevant to contemporary China studies, with the capacity to refine and publish results. Exemplary scholarly achievement and strong future promise in one or more areas of contemporary China studies: Chinese foreign policy and international relations; security and defence issues; and/or Chinese domestic politics. A clear commitment to public engagement, including the readiness to brief government, business and the broader policy community. Experience or willingness to engage in media appearances, policy writing, and opinion writing. Willingness to take part in public-facing activities such as workshops, seminars, and public events. Excellent English-language communication skills, both written and spoken. Professional integrity and collegiality, including high standards of reliability, decorum, and joint work. *** The successful candidate will be required to complete a Police Check, an academic qualification check and any other relevant background checks required for the role. Application Requirements Applicants must submit an application package online including: 1. Letter of Application (maximum two pages) summarising the applicant’s interest in the fellowship, detail relevant qualifications and research agenda and confirm Australian citizenship or Australian permanent residency status. 2. Curriculum vitae which prrovides candidate's current contact information and details academic credentials, professional experience, research and publication record. 3. References which include the names, title(s), and email of three persons who can knowledgeably speak to the candidate's academic qualifications and professional character. One of the references must be the candidate's primary PhD advisor. Additional supporting documentation may be requested from shortlisted candidates. Application Timeline: Applications Close: Thursday15 October 2026 at 11:59 p.m. (AEDT) Shortlisted candidates contacted: November 2026 Successful candidate notified: December 2026 Position commences: 2027 (prior to 1 June 2027, date to be agreed) For general enquiries about the role, please contact the Mirna Alaaiddin at mirna.alaaiddin@mq.edu.au We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 15/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Expression-of-Interest---Teaching-Associate--School-of-Computing_R000023452": {
      "title": "Expression of Interest – Teaching Associate, School of Computing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPRIMARY DETAIL DISCOVER, CREATE, INNOVATE  The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University delivers quality education to enable our students to reach their full potential, and work with our communities to discover, create and innovate with sustainability at our core.   THE ROLE  The School of Computing is inviting expressions of interest for inclusion within our casual academic pool for 2026.   For your application to be considered for Session 2 2026, please register your Expression of Interest (EOI) by Friday 12th June 2026 by uploading your relevant qualifications and requested details via the Workday application process. The School of Computing offers a range of undergraduate and postgraduate units to students completing courses in the Faculty of Science and Engineering, as well as service and elective units to students from across the campus. We employ casual academic staff to support our teaching of these courses.   We are currently inviting Expressions of interest (EOIs) from appropriately qualified individuals who demonstrate the following skills, qualifications, and experience.   ESSENTIAL CRITERIA   Completed Bachelor and/or Master’s degree in Computing, or a closely related discipline.  Sufficient discipline-specific knowledge  An understanding and appreciation of scholarly teaching  Excellent communication skills  Proven ability to interact effectively with students, staff and the community     TO APPLY  All interested applicants are required to upload a copy of their CV , copy of degree / testamur and a cover letter addressing the above criteria as part of the EOI process.  To assist in the review process, please complete this survey Qualtrics Survey | Qualtrics Experience Management (this survey is compulsory)   After initial review, applicants will be asked to prepare a short video to demonstrate their teaching style. If you are already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health): Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs.  If you are NOT currently part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health): click the 'Apply' button.  *Please note that this position is not available for visa sponsorship and the successful applicant must have work rights in Australia*   Position Enquiries: Elizabeth Bignucolo, Sessional Academic Staff Coordinator  at elizabeth.bignucolo@mq.edu.au Applications Close: Thursday, 31st of December 2026 11:59 pm (AEST) We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 31/12/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Lecturer-in-Engineering--Research-and-Teaching-_R000024191": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Engineering (Research and Teaching)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n- Salary package:  $127,138 - $150,425 (Level B.1 – B.6) plus 17% employer's superannuation contribution and annual leave loading. - Three full-time, continuing roles - Based at Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde The School of Engineering is seeking three dynamic, early-to-mid-career rising stars to join us as Lecturers (Level B) . We have the flexibility to appoint across Civil, Mechanical and Mechatronic Engineering.  We are looking for outstanding academics who bridge the gap between engineering theory and practical execution. While academic rigor is essential, we are explicitly looking for individuals who know how to build engineering artifacts. You possess strong practical engineering skills, a passion for prototyping, design, or implementation, and the ability to inspire students through hands-on, project-based education. In these roles, you will contribute to our rapidly growing undergraduate and postgraduate programs, supervise Higher Degree by Research (HDR) students, and develop an impactful, independent research profile that translates innovative ideas into tangible, real-world solutions. These roles are full-time, continuing (tenure-track) positions, based at our Wallumattagal (North Ryde) Campus in Sydney. About Us The School of Engineering at Macquarie University is rapidly expanding the capacity and impact of its research and education frameworks. As a comprehensive school, our expertise spans civil, environmental, mechanical, mechatronic, biomedical, electrical, and electronic engineering. This year, we established our operations in a brand-new, $150 million education and research precinct: the Engineering Innovation Building. This facility features state-of-the-art spaces designed specifically for immersive, team-based design and manufacturing projects, alongside specialist laboratories hosting our highly ranked research groups. As part of the Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE), we nurture the next generation of technology innovators, supporting nearly 9,000 students across our programs. Our research and teaching directly address the critical challenges faced by global society—including infrastructure resilience, autonomous systems, future materials, and sustainable energy. To Apply To be considered for this position, candidates must submit a copy of their curriculum vitae alongside a statement of no more than five pages addressing the selection criteria outlined below. Essential criteria (Lecturer Level B) To be successful, candidates will need to demonstrate their capability across the following areas: A PhD in Civil, Mechanical, Mechatronic, or a closely related engineering discipline. Demonstrated hands-on engineering skills with a track record of physical prototyping, experimental system design, field testing, or practical project execution. Evidence of capability to design and deliver engaging, high-quality, project-led learning experiences that develop both the technical and practical competencies of engineering students. A developing or established track record of quality publications and a clear trajectory for securing external research funding or industry partnerships. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively across disciplinary boundaries and work with industry partners. The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion. *This position requires a criminal history and qualifications check. Applications Close: Sunday 18th of October at 11:59pm (AEST). We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role please contact Professor Gordon Wyeth, Dean of School of Engineering: fse.eng-dean@mq.edu.au . Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 18/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Associate-Professor-of-Engineering_R000024150": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n- Salary package:  $186,433 - $205,067 (Level D.1 – D.4) plus 17% employer's superannuation contribution and annual leave loading. - Full-time, continuing role - Based at Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde About the Role The School of Engineering invites applications for an Associate Professor in Civil Engineering (Teaching and Research) with a specialization in Transport Engineering . In this role, you will deliver high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate education, supervise Higher Degree by Research (HDR) students, secure competitive research funding, and strengthen Macquarie University’s strategic connections within the transport industry. The successful applicant will have a proven track record of creating engaging learning experiences for students and driving real-world impact through their research. We are seeking candidates with expertise in making transportation systems efficient, reliable, affordable, and sustainable. Areas of particular interest include network planning and modelling, safety, public transport analysis, and environmental modelling. This is a full-time, continuing (tenure-track) position based at our Wallumattagal (North Ryde) Campus in Sydney. About Us The School of Engineering at Macquarie University is rapidly expanding the capacity and impact of its research and education frameworks. As a comprehensive school, our expertise spans civil, environmental, mechanical, mechatronic, biomedical, electrical, and electronic engineering. This year, we established our operations in a brand-new, $150 million education and research precinct: the Engineering Innovation Building. This facility features state-of-the-art spaces designed specifically for project- and team-based learning, alongside specialist laboratories hosting our highly ranked research groups. As part of the Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE), we nurture the next generation of technology innovators, supporting nearly 9,000 students across our programs. Our research and teaching directly address the critical challenges faced by global society—including the changing environment, future materials, sustainable fuels, and biotechnology. To Apply To be considered for this position, candidates must submit a copy of their curriculum vitae alongside a statement of no more than five pages addressing the selection criteria outlined below. Essential criteria for appointment at Associate Professor (Level D) A PhD in Civil Engineering, Transport Engineering, or a closely related discipline. A demonstrated and growing national and international reputation for academic excellence, evidenced by independent, innovative, and sustained contributions to research and education in transport engineering. Demonstrated ability to lead, design, and deliver high-quality curriculum and transformative teaching and learning experiences, with a track record of high student satisfaction and engagement. Proven leadership in securing and managing competitive research grants (e.g., ARC) and/or industry-funded projects, leading to high-impact publications and tangible socio-economic or policy outcomes. A sustained track record of successful Higher Degree Research (HDR) supervision to completion, and a commitment to mentoring candidates toward successful academic or industry careers. Demonstrated leadership in contributing to a positive, collaborative, and inclusive workplace culture that values diversity of thought, equity, and the professional development of colleagues. Outstanding communication, negotiation, and interpersonal skills, with a proven ability to build strategic partnerships and work effectively with internal institutional stakeholders and external industry or government partners. The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion. *This position requires a criminal history and qualifications check. Applications Close: Sunday 18th of October 2026 at 11:59pm (AEST). We welcome applications from international candidates. We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role please contact Professor Gordon Wyeth, Dean of School of Engineering: fse.eng-dean@mq.edu.au Pre-Employment Checks  Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 18/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where