    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Lecturer---Senior-Lecturer---Associate-Professor-in-Computer-Science_R000024189-1": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer / Associate Professor in Computer Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAcademic Level: Lecturer (Level B), Senior Lecturer (Level C), or Associate Professor (Level D) Salary Package: $127,138 - $205,067 plus 17% employer's superannuation and annual leave loading Appointment Type : Full-time, continuing Location: Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Macquarie University is seeking an outstanding academic to join the School of Computing in the Faculty of Science and Engineering. This is an open-rank appointment , with the successful candidate appointed at Lecturer (Level B), Senior Lecturer (Level C), or Associate Professor (Level D) depending on their qualifications, experience, academic achievements and leadership profile. We welcome applications from talented academics working across any major area of Computer Science . Areas of particular interest include, but are not limited to: Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning Generative AI, Foundation Models and Large Language Models Data Science and Data Analytics Data Management and Information Retrieval Cybersecurity, Privacy and Trust Software Engineering and Programming Languages Computer Systems and Architecture Cloud, Edge and Distributed Computing Computer Networks and Internet Technologies Human-Computer Interaction and Human-Centred Computing Computer Vision and Multimedia Natural Language Processing Robotics and Autonomous Systems Algorithms, Optimisation and Theoretical Computer Science Responsible, Trustworthy and Secure Computing Computational Science and interdisciplinary applications of computing Emerging areas of Computer Science We are particularly interested in candidates undertaking ambitious, high-quality and impactful research , with the potential to strengthen and expand the School's research capabilities and contribute to its national and international profile. The successful candidate will contribute to research, teaching and academic service appropriate to their level of appointment. This may include developing, teaching and convening undergraduate and postgraduate units, supervising Higher Degree Research students, building research collaborations, attracting external research funding, engaging with industry and government, and contributing to academic leadership within the School, Faculty and University. We encourage applications from candidates with both established and emerging research profiles, including talented early-career academics demonstrating an exceptional trajectory. About Us You will be joining a growing School of Computing in the Faculty of Science and Engineering with a fast-rising international reputation. The School is home to more than 60 academic staff, over 150 research students, and close to 3,500 undergraduate and postgraduate coursework students. It offers a broad range of contemporary undergraduate and postgraduate programs and has a strong and growing research culture. The School provides a collaborative environment in which academics are encouraged to pursue ambitious research agendas, develop interdisciplinary and industry partnerships, contribute to innovative teaching, and build internationally recognised academic careers. This appointment represents an opportunity for an outstanding academic to contribute to the next phase of growth and development of Computer Science at Macquarie University. About You – Selection Criteria The successful candidate will be an ambitious and collegial academic with a strong commitment to research and education. We are looking for candidates who can demonstrate achievement and potential relative to their career stage and the academic level for which they are being considered . Selection Criteria – All Applicants (Levels B, C and D) Applicants at all levels should demonstrate: A PhD in Computer Science, Computing, or a closely related discipline. A strong and coherent research program in one or more areas of contemporary Computer Science. A high-quality research publication record, relative to career stage and opportunity, demonstrated through publications in respected international journals, conferences or other recognised scholarly venues appropriate to the candidate's field. Evidence of the quality, originality, significance or potential impact of their research. Demonstrated capability and commitment to delivering high-quality and innovative teaching at undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels. Capacity to contribute to curriculum development and teaching in areas relevant to the School's undergraduate and postgraduate programs. Evidence of the ability to supervise, or the potential to successfully supervise, Higher Degree Research students. Evidence of the ability to develop research collaborations within academia and/or with industry, government or other external partners. Evidence of success, or clear potential for success, in attracting external research funding appropriate to career stage. High-level oral and written communication skills, with demonstrated ability to work effectively and collegially with students, academic and professional staff, collaborators and external stakeholders. A demonstrated commitment to contributing positively to an inclusive, collaborative and high-performing academic environment. Industry engagement, interdisciplinary research, international collaboration, entrepreneurship, translation or demonstrated research impact beyond academia will be highly regarded. Additional Selection Criteria – Senior Lecturer (Level C) Candidates seeking appointment at Senior Lecturer (Level C) should, in addition to the criteria above, demonstrate: An established and internationally recognised research profile, with a sustained record of high-quality research outputs and evidence of increasing research influence and impact. A demonstrated record of successful supervision of Higher Degree Research students, including contribution to the development of research students and early-career researchers. A demonstrated record of attracting external research funding, or substantial evidence of the capacity to lead competitive research funding applications and funded research projects. Evidence of leadership in research, teaching, curriculum development, academic programs, research groups, professional activities, or other areas relevant to the School. A demonstrated capacity to develop and lead productive research collaborations and contribute to building research capability within a School or broader academic environment. Evidence of a growing national and international reputation in the candidate's field. Additional Selection Criteria – Associate Professor (Level D) Candidates seeking appointment at Associate Professor (Level D) should, in addition to the criteria above, demonstrate: A distinguished and internationally recognised research profile, with a sustained record of outstanding scholarly achievement, research influence and impact. A substantial record of research leadership, including leadership of significant research programs, teams, centres, networks or major collaborative initiatives. A strong record of attracting and leading significant external research funding from competitive, government, industry or other sources. A strong record of successful Higher Degree Research supervision and research mentorship, including demonstrated contribution to developing research students, early-career academics and research capability. Significant academic leadership in areas such as research strategy, education, curriculum, academic programs, organisational development, external engagement or professional leadership. Demonstrated ability to build strategic collaborations with leading national and international researchers, industry, government and/or other external partners. Evidence of a strong national and international standing in the candidate's discipline and the capacity to enhance the research reputation, visibility and impact of the School of Computing and Macquarie University. Demonstrated capacity to provide intellectual and academic leadership and to contribute strategically to the future development of the School. How to Apply To be considered for this position, please submit: your curriculum vitae; a cover letter outlining your interest in the position and the academic level for which you wish to be considered; and a statement addressing how your experience and achievements align with the relevant selection criteria. Candidates may be considered for appointment at a level different from the level nominated in their application where their qualifications, experience and achievements support such consideration. Applications Close: Thursday 15th October at 11:59pm (AEST). This role requires a police/criminal history check. The role may also require a Defence Trade Controls Act 2012 section 10A permit, and appointment will be subject to satisfying all requirements associated with that permit where applicable. Applications will be considered holistically and with regard to career stage and opportunity. Candidates are encouraged to apply even where they do not meet every individual criterion. The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion. Enquiries For enquiries or a confidential conversation about the role, please contact:  Professor Amin Beheshti - School of Computing, Macquarie University - amin.beheshti@mq.edu.au . Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Take a look at the fabulous staff benefits on offer when you work at Macquarie University: Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks  Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 15/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
